# Nexus Health (Hospital Blood Report Analyzer)

Django 6 + DRF + JWT hospital demo: patients (appointments, lab uploads), doctors (schedule, remarks), admins (verification, integrations). PostgreSQL in CI/production; SQLite allowed locally unless `REQUIRE_POSTGRES=True`.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `app/` | Models, views, serializers, permissions, services, tests |
| `config/` | `settings.py`, root `urls.py`, WSGI |
| `templates/` | Role dashboards, auth, `base_dashboard.html` |
| `static/css/nexus-theme.css` | Shared theme |
| `scripts/` | Render smoke, seed, sync helpers |
| `docs/hackathon/n8n/` | n8n workflow JSON |

## Domain rules (do not break)

- Custom `User` with roles: `ADMIN`, `DOCTOR`, `PATIENT` — use `app.permissions` (`IsAdmin`, `IsDoctor`, `IsPatient`, `IsDoctorOrAdmin`).
- Appointments: anti–double-booking, 30-minute minimum lead time, IDs like `APT-YYYY-NNNNNN`.
- Blood reports: local media, optional Google Drive, n8n webhook on upload; callback updates `HealthReport` / `ai_analysis`.
- Secrets and integration config live in env / `IntegrationConfig`, never hard-coded in source.

## Before finishing changes

- Run targeted tests: `python manage.py test app --verbosity 2`
- CI also runs `ruff check` (F rules on key files), `manage.py check --deploy`, and `pip-audit`
